<h2 id="why-your-small-business-deserves-better-email-than-gmail" tabindex="-1">Why your small business deserves better email than Gmail</h2><p>You started a business to do something that matters. Your email service should support that mission, not undermine it with ads, surveillance, and a service that treat <em>you</em> like the product. Fastmail is email built for people who take their work seriously, and that includes the 5-person consultancy as much as the 50-person agency.</p><h2 id="real-reliability-means-you-can-stop-thinking-about-email" tabindex="-1">Real reliability means you can stop thinking about email</h2><p>Gmail is free because you’re the inventory, not the customer. When something breaks or gets blocked, you’re filing tickets into a void. Fastmail’s support is staffed by actual humans who understand email deeply and respond quickly because <em>your</em> subscription pays their salary, not advertisers. One Hacker News commenter put it simply:</p><blockquote> <p><em>“Fastmail just works. I’ve been using it for my business for years and have never had downtime that wasn’t scheduled maintenance.”</em></p> </blockquote><p>That kind of boring reliability is exactly what your business needs. Email should be infrastructure you forget about because it simply works.</p><h2 id="your-domain-your-identity-your-control" tabindex="-1">Your domain, your identity, your control</h2><p>Custom domains are essential for professional email. Fastmail makes domain setup straightforward and supports multiple domains per account, so you can manage client-specific addresses or separate projects without juggling multiple services. The interface for managing aliases and domain-specific identities is thoughtful rather than buried in settings hell. You own your domain, which means you own your business identity. If you ever want to move, you take your email address with you. No lock-in, no vendor hostage situations.</p><h2 id="privacy-as-a-business-advantage-not-a-luxury" tabindex="-1">Privacy as a business advantage, not a luxury</h2><p>When you’re handling client communications, vendor contracts, or financial information, surveillance-based email is a liability. Fastmail’s business model is transparent: you pay money, you get email, nobody reads your messages to sell you things. As one Reddit user noted:</p><blockquote> <p><em>“Switched our studio to Fastmail specifically because we were uncomfortable with Google scanning client communications for ad targeting. Fastmail’s privacy approach just made sense for a professional service.”</em></p> </blockquote><h2 id="migration-is-easier-than-you-think" tabindex="-1">Migration is easier than you think</h2><p>The biggest barrier to switching is often inertia. Fastmail’s migration tools handle the heavy lifting of moving your existing email, contacts, and calendars. The interface is genuinely faster and more powerful than Gmail, with better search, better filters, better keyboard shortcuts for those of us who live in our inbox. Shared accounts and team features work without the enterprise-tier pricing nonsense. You can start with one account, prove it works, then move the team over without drama.</p><p>Small businesses succeed when they make dozens of small but smart decisions that compound over time, like choosing email that respects your intelligence, protects your privacy, and actually works reliably.</p><p>Fastmail costs money because quality costs money. Your business is worth it.</p>